---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import fredPortrait from "../../../../assets/fred.jpg";

/*
 * Section 3 — who you're working with. The section this page cannot ship without.
 *
 * THE PORTRAIT IS NOT DECORATION AND THE COPY FILE SAYS SO: an unverifiable claim about
 * a named person, with no face attached, reads worse than no section at all. It is the
 * only image on the whole page. If the image ever fails to resolve, fix the image —
 * do not ship the section without it.
 *
 * THIS IS THE LONG VERSION OF THE HOMEPAGE FOUNDER STRIP, and the two share their
 * heading, their body paragraph and their chips word for word. sections/home/
 * FounderStripSection.astro is the condensed one — it drops the second paragraph
 * because the homepage runs a tight argument that a full founder section would
 * interrupt. THEY HAVE TO STAY IN SYNC: a change to the years, the products or the
 * chips here is wrong on the homepage the same day, and there is no shared constant
 * because it is prose, not data.
 *
 * THREE CHIPS, NOT FOUR. Approved copy sets "15+ years engineering · Two products
 * founded and shipped · Metro Vancouver · Founder-led delivery". Fredrick's instruction
 * of Aug 25 2026 removes the location and everything like it from the visible site,
 * confirmed again on Aug 26 when this page was planned. The homepage strip lost the same
 * chip on the same instruction. Two other places on this page lost the same thing — the
 * hero subhead and section 6's location paragraph. Do not restore one alone.
 *
 * VOICE: written ABOUT Fredrick, never by him, and this is the one rule the copy file
 * gives for the whole page. "We" throughout, Fredrick named once in the third person.
 * That single choice is what makes the page read as a company with a founder rather than
 * a person with a website. It must not drift into first person — not here, and not in
 * the second paragraph, which is the one most likely to attract an "I".
 *
 * "FOUNDED AND SHIPPED" IS DELIBERATE AND MUST NOT BE INFLATED. The copy file calls it
 * unarguable, and anything stronger — "built and scaled", "grew", "successful" — invites
 * a question this page cannot answer. Both products are already named on the homepage,
 * so naming them here is not new exposure.
 */

const chips = [
  "15+ years engineering",
  "Two products founded and shipped",
  "Founder-led delivery",
];
---

<section class="section section--surface founder" id="who-youre-working-with">
  <div class="container founder__inner">
    {/* Cropped to a circle by `object-fit: cover`, which is doing real work here:
        assets/fred.jpg is 520x650, not square, so cover trims equal strips off the top
        and bottom and centres what is left. Measured on the built page — the face lands
        centred. A replacement portrait with the subject off-centre vertically will crop
        badly and the CSS cannot fix it; crop the source instead.

        The homepage's FounderStripSection carries an older version of this note claiming
        the source is square and must be 1:1. It is not, and never was. */}
    <Image
      src={fredPortrait}
      alt="Fredrick, founder of ArkSystems"
      widths={[220, 440]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 140px, 220px"
      class="founder__portrait"
    />

    <div class="founder__copy">
      <h2 class="section__title founder__title">
        You work directly with the people who build your system.
      </h2>

      <p class="founder__body">
        ArkSystems is led by its founder, Fredrick, who spent more than fifteen years in
        software engineering, solution architecture, systems integration and cloud
        infrastructure, and who founded and shipped two technology products, FoodyGuru
        and YoseeAI.
      </p>

      <p class="founder__body founder__body--second">
        That matters to you in two ways. You deal with the people building the thing
        &mdash; there is no account manager, and no junior consultant taking over once the
        work is sold. And the parts that usually get skipped are the parts we&rsquo;ve had
        to care about: what a system costs to run, whether it stays up, and whether anyone
        actually uses it a month later.
      </p>

      <ul class="founder__chips">
        {chips.map((chip) => <li class="founder__chip">{chip}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .founder__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .founder__portrait {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 6px solid var(--ark-white);
    box-shadow: var(--ark-raised);
  }

  .founder__title {
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .founder__body {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-size: var(--ark-body);
    line-height: var(--ark-lh-body);
    color: var(--ark-body-ink);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .founder__body--second {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .founder__chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 26px;
  }

  .founder__chip {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ark-olive);
    background: var(--ark-green-soft);
    border-radius: var(--ark-radius-pill);
    padding: 5px 14px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    /* Portrait above, centred. At 390px a 140px circle beside text leaves the text about
     * 190px wide, which wraps the heading to six lines. */
    .founder__inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      justify-items: center;
      gap: 24px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .founder__portrait {
      width: 140px;
      height: 140px;
      border-width: 5px;
    }

    .founder__title {
      max-width: 20ch;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    /* Prose keeps its left edge even though the block centres — same rule as everywhere
     * else on the site. */
    .founder__body {
      text-align: left;
      max-width: 42ch;
      margin-inline: auto;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .founder__chips {
      justify-content: center;
    }
  }
</style>
